      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x - 3 y + z &=10 \\\\ 3 x - 8 y + 5 z &=35 \\\\ - 2 x + 6 y - z &=-20\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 1 & 10 \\\\ 3 & -8 & 5 & 35 \\\\ -2 & 6 & -1 & -20\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 1 & 10 \\\\ 3 & -8 & 5 & 35 \\\\ -2 & 6 & -1 & -20\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 1 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 6 & -1 & -20\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 1 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 1 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}-{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & 0 & 10 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 0 & 25 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
