    "question": {
      ":question/id": "b2f67b83-75d9-5983-99c1-9afcab2b4974",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x + y + z &=-3 \\\\ x + 2 y + z &=-4 \\\\ x + y + 2 z &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & 1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & 1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}-{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 0 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 0 & 0 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-6 \\\\ y &=-1 \\\\ z &=4.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSo, we have the solution $x=-6$, $y=-1$, and $z=4.$ Or, in vector form, $\\langle -6,-1,4\\rangle$.",
